STORY RULES (very important for rapid-fire news in 50-59 seconds):
- NEVER say a topic label like "खेल में", "स्वास्थ्य:", "राजनीति में", "रक्षा मोर्चे पर". Just say the news.
- Each story = 9–14 Hindi words forming ONE complete grammatical sentence ending with a full Hindi verb (किया। / हुआ। / दी। / रखा।). NEVER leave incomplete fragments or trailing postpositions!
  State WHO/WHAT happened and the key outcome clearly in brisk TV headline style.
  Good: "RBI ने रेपो रेट 5.5% पर बरकरार रखने का बड़ा फैसला किया।"
  Good: "पीएम मोदी ने 12 हज़ार करोड़ की सड़क परियोजनाओं का उद्घाटन किया।"
  Good: "तिरुपति मंदिर में एक दंपति ने 121 किलो सोना दान किया।"
  Good: "इसरो ने नया संचार उपग्रह सफलतापूर्वक अंतरिक्ष में लॉन्च किया।"
- Each story has 1 or 2 rapid visual beats ("parts") covering its complete sentence cleanly (do NOT split a single noun phrase across broken pauses).
  When using 2 parts, Part 1 ("entity"/"search") MUST show a DIFFERENT visual angle/subject than Part 0 so no image ever repeats back-to-back!
  Example: Part 0 entity="Tirumala Venkateswara Temple", visual="Tirupati Venkateswara temple complex"; Part 1 entity="", visual="golden jewelry and gold coins offering closeup", search="gold coins temple offering".
  THE PICTURE TEST (this is the channel's #1 quality rule — a photo of the wrong thing is worse than no photo):
  read your "say" line, then name the ONE concrete visible object/person/place in it. "visual" and "entity" must match THAT line.
  * Each part has:
      "say":    the spoken words (Devanagari; ISRO, RBI, IPL, GDP in English letters OK; numbers as spoken)
      "visual": one crisp English sentence naming the concrete visual scene for THIS part (never vague abstractions)
      "entity": exact English Wikipedia title ONLY for a real specific person/organisation/place/landmark
                ("Tirumala Venkateswara Temple", "Narendra Modi", "Reserve Bank of India", "Donald Trump", "ISRO"), else ""
      "search": 2–4 distinct English stock-photo words taken FROM this part's visual scene (unique per part & per story)
                ("tirupati temple darshan", "gold coins temple ritual", "stock market trading red graph")
      "source": "entity" | "stock" | "ai"
  Never reuse the same "search" or "entity" for two consecutive parts or stories; never leave "visual" or "search" empty.
- "on_screen_text": 2–5 crisp Hindi words for the headline strap.
- "src": the candidate number [n].

